"Hannah Elber is an A-rank Adjuster who stabilizes and freezes isolated patches of reality."
"Her first spell was a basic mobile barrier, which grew into her Bubble of Patient Waiting."
"She has brown hair, often braided around her head like a crown or in two French braids."
"She wears combat boots and a blue motorcycle jacket that sparkles with magic when active."
"Her mother is the Gloom, a Sky Shaper who lives in London, and Hannah looks like her."
"Her birthday is February 13."
"She went to superhero school on Anesidora with Cly Zhao, her best friend, and Keiko Velra."
"She and Keiko Velra were classmates but didn't really mesh."
"Her college motto was Happy to help; later she would say We could have done that better."
"She was Arjun Thomas's battlefield support, the pair hired by Illinois to work in Chicago."
"She froze eight-year-old Alden Thorn in a bubble, saved his toy wombat and wrote him notes."
"She blamed herself for the Thorn deaths, saying she stabilized the eighth floor, not the seventh."
"She keeps a bright public persona and a Hero Hannah voice."
"She left Alden's aunt a note: call me if you or Alden ever need anything."
"She listed Alden as a priority contact and hosted his summer visits to Anesidora each year."
"She put Argold under Alden's name for his visits."
"Illinois did not renew her and Arjun's contracts after the Body Drainer incident."
"She has used her bubble on hundreds; only three besides Alden stayed conscious, all Avowed kids."
"For years she supported a middle-aged hero in Jakarta who heats and cools small areas."
"She once sat with Alden on a barrier platform in a duck pond."
"She really wanted her life to matter."
"She went on her fourth quest summons and never came back."
"After half a year missing she was presumed dead, and a funeral was held on Anesidora."
"Her memorial service was at Celena North University in Apex, organized partly by Cly Zhao."
"Alden guesses she died in a demon disaster."
